  "term": "writer’s cramp",
  "definition": "Writer’s cramp is a focal dystonic disorder, meaning a condition in which dystonia mainly affects one specific body area rather than the whole body. It is an example of a dystonic disorder in which dystonia is the main feature of the condition.",
